BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 748.0 Td (  The Guardian of First Trust held waters that, when released downstream, would multiply threefo) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 738.0 Td (    ld in the valley below. But this guardian could never drink from their own waters-only what ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 728.0 Td (    flowed back from below could quench their thirst.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 718.0 Td (  ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 708.0 Td (  The Guardian of Return received these multiplied waters, abundant and life-giving. Yet they to) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 698.0 Td (    o faced a choice: to keep all the bounty, or send some portion back upstream.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 688.0 Td (  ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 678.0 Td (  For many seasons, the guardians withheld their waters, and both rivers ran dry. The valley wit) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 668.0 Td (    hered.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 658.0 Td (  ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 648.0 Td (  Then one day, the Guardian of First Trust released a modest portion, trusting in reciprocity. ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 638.0 Td (    The waters multiplied in the valley, and the Guardian of Return, seeing this gift, sent back) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 628.0 Td (     a fair share. Both rivers began to flow.) Tj ET
