BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 518.0 Td (      # The Myth of the Twin Rivers) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 508.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 498.0 Td (      In the beginning, two rivers flowed from separate mountains-the River of First Trust and t) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 488.0 Td (        he River of Return. Each was tended by a guardian spirit.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 478.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 468.0 Td (      The Guardian of First Trust held waters that, when released downstream, would multiply thr) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 458.0 Td (        eefold in the valley below. But this guardian could never drink from their own waters-on) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 448.0 Td (        ly what flowed back from below could quench their thirst.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 438.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 428.0 Td (      The Guardian of Return received these multiplied waters, abundant and life-giving. Yet the) Tj ET
