BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 288.0 Td (      # The Myth of the Twin Rivers) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 278.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 268.0 Td (      In the beginning, two rivers flowed from separate mountains-the River of First Trust and t) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 258.0 Td (        he River of Return. Each was tended by a guardian spirit.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 248.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 238.0 Td (      The Guardian of First Trust held waters that, when released downstream, would multiply thr) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 228.0 Td (        eefold in the valley below. But this guardian could never drink from their own waters-on) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 218.0 Td (        ly what flowed back from below could quench their thirst.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 208.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 198.0 Td (      The Guardian of Return received these multiplied waters, abundant and life-giving. Yet the) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 188.0 Td (        y too faced a choice: to keep all the bounty, or send some portion back upstream.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 178.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 168.0 Td (      For many seasons, the guardians withheld their waters, and both rivers ran dry. The valley) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 158.0 Td (         withered.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 148.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 138.0 Td (      Then one day, the Guardian of First Trust released a modest portion, trusting in reciproci) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 128.0 Td (        ty. The waters multiplied in the valley, and the Guardian of Return, seeing this gift, s) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 118.0 Td (        ent back a fair share. Both rivers began to flow.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 108.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 98.0 Td (      They learned that trust begets abundance, and reciprocity sustains it. The more First Trus) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 88.0 Td (        t released, the more flourished in the valley-and the more Return sent back, the more bo) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 78.0 Td (        th guardians thrived.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 68.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 58.0 Td (      Thus the valley bloomed eternal, fed by the sacred cycle of trust and return, where giving) Tj ET
