BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 578.0 Td (      # The Myth of the Flowing River) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 568.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 558.0 Td (      In ancient times, two villages stood on opposite banks of a sacred river. Each dawn, the R) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 548.0 Td (        iver Spirit granted the upstream village five silver stones. The villagers faced a choic) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 538.0 Td (        e: keep the stones, or cast them into the flowing waters.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 528.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 518.0 Td (      When stones touched the river, they multiplied threefold by the time they reached the down) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 508.0 Td (        stream village. Those who received the stones could then choose: keep all the bounty, or) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 498.0 Td (         return some upstream as gratitude.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 488.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 478.0 Td (      At first, the upstream village hoarded their stones, sending nothing. Both villages remain) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 468.0 Td (        ed poor. Then one brave elder cast all five stones into the current. Downstream rejoiced) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 458.0 Td (         at receiving fifteen stones, and in gratitude, returned eight upstream.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 448.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 438.0 Td (      The elder learned: by giving five and receiving eight back, both villages prospered. When ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 428.0 Td (        downstream returned generously, trust grew like roots intertwining beneath the water.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 418.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 408.0 Td (      But when downstream grew greedy and returned nothing, the flow ceased. The river taught th) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 398.0 Td (        at prosperity flows both ways-the gift must complete its circle.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 388.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 378.0 Td (      The wisest generation learned balance: send enough to create abundance, return enough to s) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 368.0 Td (        ustain trust. For the river's magic lies not in the stones themselves, but in the curren) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 358.0 Td (        t of reciprocity that carries them endlessly between shores, enriching all who honor the) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 348.0 Td (         flow.) Tj ET
