BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 318.0 Td (      # The Tale of the River and the Rain) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 308.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 298.0 Td (      In the beginning, the River and the Rain lived separately. The Rain dwelt in clouds above,) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 288.0 Td (         holding precious waters. The River flowed below, carrying life to the valleys.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 278.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 268.0 Td (      One day, the Great Spirit spoke: "You are kin, yet divided. Share your gifts, and abundanc) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 258.0 Td (        e shall multiply.") Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 248.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 238.0 Td (      The Rain was uncertain. "If I release my waters to the River below, what if nothing return) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 228.0 Td (        s?") Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 218.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 208.0 Td (      But the Rain took courage and let its waters fall. When they touched the River, they tripl) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 198.0 Td (        ed in abundance. The valley bloomed. The creatures drank. Life flourished.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 188.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 178.0 Td (      The River, now overflowing with plenty, understood its duty. Through evaporation, it retur) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 168.0 Td (        ned waters skyward, replenishing the Rain's clouds. Not equal to what it received-the Ri) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 158.0 Td (        ver needed sustenance too-but enough to honor the Rain's trust and ensure future gifts.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 148.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 138.0 Td (      Season after season, they continued this sacred exchange. When the Rain gave generously, t) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 128.0 Td (        he River returned faithfully. Both prospered. The valley thrived.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 118.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 108.0 Td (      But when either grew selfish-the Rain withholding or the River returning nothing-drought d) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 98.0 Td (        escended upon them both.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 88.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 78.0 Td (      Thus the Great Spirit taught: *Trust given and honored multiplies; trust broken diminishes) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 68.0 Td (         all.*) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 58.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
