BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 398.0 Td (      # The Myth of the Twin Springs) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 388.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 378.0 Td (      In the beginning, two springs emerged from the mountain-one in the valley of Dawn, one in ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 368.0 Td (        the valley of Dusk. Each spring gave its keeper five cups of water daily.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 358.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 348.0 Td (      The Keeper of Dawn discovered that when she poured water into the river flowing toward Dus) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 338.0 Td (        k, the waters multiplied threefold by the time they arrived. The Keeper of Dusk could th) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 328.0 Td (        en choose what to send back upstream.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 318.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 308.0 Td (      At first, Dawn was fearful. "If I send my water away, I may receive nothing in return and ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 298.0 Td (        suffer thirst." So she sent but one cup. Dusk, receiving three cups, returned one out of) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 288.0 Td (         gratitude.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 278.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 268.0 Td (      Seasons passed. Dawn began to trust, sending more. When she sent three cups, Dusk received) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 258.0 Td (         nine-enough for both to flourish. Dusk, seeing Dawn's faith, returned five cups. Both v) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 248.0 Td (        alleys bloomed.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 238.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 228.0 Td (      But in times when Dawn held back in fear, or when Dusk kept all for himself, the springs g) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 218.0 Td (        rew cold and diminished. The mountain itself seemed to know.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 208.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 198.0 Td (      The elders say: *Prosperity flows in circles, not lines. The spring that gives freely shal) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 188.0 Td (        l never run dry, and the hand that returns with gratitude shall always be filled.*) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 178.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
